      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T18:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oof. I hit this *all* the time.\n\nSo I\u0027ve been told that the great printk rework was going to resolve this, but there\u0027s apparently some work still to do on the console driver.\n\nSo SCHED_WARN_ON() has since been dropped upstream, but I still trip over this issue there. I wonder if its something we should propose upstream for WARN_ON in general?",
      "revId": "fb1539c24b2dc9aca66a0dffb2b06d915ec32d27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e6a2aac_8f658ef1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869780
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T19:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The printk() maintainers are working on printk() changes that should make this CL superfluous in the future. From https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20251028184537.GC3419281@noisy.programming.kicks-ass.net/:\n```\nThe printk() people have been working on fixing this for a long while\nand I think they\u0027re close. All the crap consoles will get threaded\nprinting while the useful consoles (serial) will get atomic printing.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "e9ab1337_bbe0cbf0",
      "revId": "fb1539c24b2dc9aca66a0dffb2b06d915ec32d27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c5d936b_6a0ea790",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T21:39:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah! I didn\u0027t realize you had already sent it upstream (though, you are excellent about working upstream, so I should have guessed :)\n\nSo, reading Peter\u0027s feedback, I don\u0027t think his concern about deferred output not making it to the console is a blocker, as for WARN_ONs we should be continuing along (though he\u0027s right that when those warnings trip, things are going bad and you likely will hit a crash shortly after, for which the deferred printing could be a problem).\n\nBut his concern about the change to \"generate absolutely atrocious code\", does give me some hesitancy.\n\nCould maybe this change be gated on CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING so make sure it doesn\u0027t impact normal GKI builds?",
      "parentUuid": "6e6a2aac_8f658ef1",
      "revId": "fb1539c24b2dc9aca66a0dffb2b06d915ec32d27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d33cfa09_0d014532",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869780
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T22:00:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need this change in builds with CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING off because otherwise SCHED_WARN_ON(true) can trigger a deadlock.\n\nI think Peter\u0027s comment is wrong. I checked the assembler code generated by this macro and it seems to me that the clang and gcc optimizers both are great at optimizing the code generated by this macro.",
      "parentUuid": "9c5d936b_6a0ea790",
      "revId": "fb1539c24b2dc9aca66a0dffb2b06d915ec32d27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51c2d483_6873895b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T22:12:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We need this change in builds with CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING off because otherwise SCHED_WARN_ON(true) can trigger a deadlock.\n\nBut it seems the trade off becomes rare crashes may not produce WARNING output at all (if you crash before we get to where printk can print), which is pretty close to the same downside as a potential deadlock (since the warnings really shouldn\u0027t be triggering).  I\u0027m open to including this (as with lockdep it is really annoying), but I\u0027m not totally sure its going to be a net improvement (other than fixing the lockdep warnings, which are totally a nuisance).\n\n\u003e I think Peter\u0027s comment is wrong. I checked the assembler code generated by this macro and it seems to me that the clang and gcc optimizers both are great at optimizing the code generated by this macro.\n\nThanks for checking this and calming my worries! Very much appreciate it.",
      "parentUuid": "d33cfa09_0d014532",
      "revId": "fb1539c24b2dc9aca66a0dffb2b06d915ec32d27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
